# PART 4 — BRAND IDENTITY & VISUAL DESIGN SYSTEM

## 4.1 Recommended Art Direction

**Design Direction:** Modern Creative Printing Studio.

The brand should feel:

- Professional.
- Creative.
- Premium.
- Trustworthy.
- Modern.
- Production-focused.

Avoid generic corporate templates, excessive gradients, excessive animations and cluttered sections.

## 4.2 Proposed Colour Palette

Use a dark neutral foundation with restrained printing-inspired CMYK accents.

| Colour | HEX | Application |
|---|---|---|
| Ink Black | #121826 | Main headings |
| Deep Navy | #17243A | Dark sections |
| Cyan | #00A6C7 | Primary brand accent |
| Magenta | #E83E8C | Creative highlights |
| Print Yellow | #F4C542 | Small highlights |
| White | #FFFFFF | Main surfaces |
| Soft Grey | #F5F7FA | Background |
| Text Grey | #667085 | Secondary text |
| Border Grey | #E5E7EB | Borders |

### Colour Usage Rules

- Cyan should be the primary interactive colour.
- Magenta and yellow should be occasional supporting accents.
- Dark neutral colours should provide visual stability.
- Avoid applying all three CMY colours to every button and section.
- Test text and background combinations for accessibility.

## 4.3 Typography

Recommended font pairing:

**English**
- Inter or Manrope.

**Nepali**
- Noto Sans Devanagari.

Typography hierarchy:

- H1: 56–68px desktop.
- H2: 36–44px desktop.
- H3: 24–30px.
- Body: 16–18px.
- Small labels: 12–14px.

Adjust sizes responsively for mobile.

## 4.4 Logo System

Prepare:

- Primary logo.
- Horizontal logo.
- Vertical logo.
- Icon-only logo.
- Dark background version.
- Light background version.
- Monochrome version.
- Favicon.
- Social media profile logo.

Preserve the existing logo if it is already established and recognizable. Redesign only after reviewing the original vector artwork.

