# PART 8 — TECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (TRD)

## 8.1 Recommended Technology Stack

### Frontend

- Next.js.
- React.
- TypeScript.
- Tailwind CSS.
- Reusable UI component library.
- Responsive image handling.

### Backend

- Next.js API / server-side application layer.
- REST API.
- PostgreSQL.
- Prisma ORM.
- Role-based authentication.
- Server-side validation.

### File Storage

S3-compatible object storage or Cloudflare R2.

Use separate storage policies for:
- Public portfolio images.
- Private customer attachments.
- Admin-only documents.

### Infrastructure

- HTTPS.
- Domain and DNS management.
- CDN.
- Production and staging environments.
- Automated database backup.
- Error monitoring.

### Architecture Decision

First identify the existing website's CMS, hosting and source code.

If the existing platform is WordPress and its content management capabilities are sufficient, improving its theme and adding custom functionality may be more economical.

If the website needs the complete custom quotation workflow, advanced admin panel and scalable architecture described here, a custom Next.js and PostgreSQL implementation is recommended.

Do not migrate platforms until the current hosting, CMS, domain and database have been audited.

