# PART 11 — CUSTOMER QUOTATION WORKFLOW

Customer Journey:

1. Customer opens the website.
2. Explores available services.
3. Selects a service.
4. Opens the quotation form.
5. Enters printing specifications.
6. Uploads artwork or reference files.
7. Submits the request.
8. Receives an enquiry reference number.
9. Administrator reviews the enquiry.
10. Administrator prepares the quotation.
11. Customer receives the quotation.
12. Customer confirms or rejects the quotation.
13. Approved work progresses through production statuses.
14. Order is marked ready and eventually completed.

A quotation is not an automatic price promise. Final pricing should be confirmed by authorized staff based on actual production specifications.

